OCGRAPH 1
DOMAIN material
# A material graph, and deliberately one that says something no PARAM block can.
#
# frac(worldPosition * 0.02) is a value that CHANGES ACROSS THE SURFACE -- bands every 50 cm in each
# axis, so a 120 cm cube shows more than two of them. That is the point: a flat colour would prove
# nothing here, because a flat colour is exactly what `PARAM baseColorFactor` already does, and a
# picture of one could not tell a working graph from a material that ignored its graph entirely and
# fell back to its own factors. A gradient can only have come from the graph.
#
# ROUGHNESS IS A TYPED LITERAL, not a wire, and that is also on purpose: it exercises the other half
# of "driven" (see compileMaterialGraph -- a MaterialOutput input counts as driven when it is LINKED
# or when a value is typed into it, and its palette pins carry no defaults precisely so a non-empty
# one is unambiguously something a person wrote). Metallic, Normal, Emissive, Occlusion and Opacity
# are left alone entirely, so they keep what this material's own .ocmat declares -- which is the
# partial-graph behaviour the whole AverAuthored split exists for.
NAME MG_Bands

NODE wp WorldPosition -420 -40
PIN wp xyz out float3

NODE rate ConstFloat3 -420 100
PIN rate value out float3 0.02,0.02,0.02

NODE scaled Multiply -200 20
PIN scaled a in float3
PIN scaled b in float3
PIN scaled result out float3

NODE bands Frac 20 20
PIN bands x in float3
PIN bands result out float3

NODE out MaterialOutput 240 -20
PIN out BaseColor in float3
PIN out Roughness in float 0.25

LINK wp.xyz scaled.a
LINK rate.value scaled.b
LINK scaled.result bands.x
LINK bands.result out.BaseColor
